# Thoughtborne -- API keys
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your API keys:
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is ignored by git and will never be committed.
#
# Thoughtborne reads its API keys from THIS file, in its install directory, and
# from nowhere else -- a Windows or shell variable of the same name is ignored.
# How a line is read:
#   - only uncommented lines count; the split is at the first `=`, and key and
#     value are trimmed of surrounding whitespace
#   - a leading `export ` is ignored, so a shell-style line works
#   - a value in one pair of matching quotes ('...' or "...") is taken literally
#     between them, and anything after the closing quote is ignored
#   - otherwise a `#` that starts the value or follows whitespace begins a
#     comment and the rest of the line is dropped (`abc#def` keeps its hash)
#   - `${OTHER}` is NOT expanded -- a value is used exactly as written
#   - the same key on two lines: the last one wins
#   - an empty value counts as no key at all

# Groq API Key (Whisper Large V3 Turbo and Large V3 -- free-tier transcription: fast / higher accuracy)
# Get your key at: https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=

# Soniox API Key (async REST and Live WebSocket streaming -- high accuracy for German)
# Get your key at: https://soniox.com
SONIOX_API_KEY=

# Developer opt-out: allow a second Thoughtborne instance to start for non-hotkey
# work (console rendering, the settings app). Leave blank in normal use -- a second
# instance normally closes itself, since global hotkeys are single-owner in Windows.
# THOUGHTBORNE_ALLOW_SECOND_INSTANCE=1
